    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "46 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-12-24 22:40:00 CST Expires: 2025-12-25 04:00:00 CST Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Target Area: Stark; Marshall Areas of dense fog have formed over portions of Stark and Marshall counties late this evening. Visibilities were at or below a quarter mile in eastern Marshall county around Varna and southward. But visibilities varied across these counties with some locations like Lacon airport having visibilities above 4 miles. Areas of dense fog should persist into early overnight, with visibilities gradually improving later tonight as increasing north to northeast winds bring drier air into the area.\nExpect rapid changes in visibility over short distances, with visibility possibly even near zero at times. Be sure to slow down if you encounter dense fog. Use low beam headlights if driving, and leave plenty of distance between you and the vehicle ahead.",
